Package: saisdata
Title: Course Data for the SAIS MIEF R Workshop
Version: 0.3.1
Authors@R:
    person("Teal", "Emery", , "lte@tealinsights.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Ready-to-use data for the two-day R workshop of the Master of
    International Economics and Finance (MIEF) at Johns Hopkins SAIS: the
    International Monetary Fund's World Economic Outlook of October 2026 as a
    tidy country panel of twelve indicators (growth, inflation, unemployment,
    the current account, GDP per person, population and the government's
    books), the whole release for countries in long form with a plain-language
    guide to its 44 indicators, a twelve-row table for first steps, the same
    source in the IMF's own layout for its two largest country groups, and the
    World Bank's country groups. One line, library(saisdata), loads them all.
    The code is MIT licensed; the data keep their own terms, set out in the
    file LICENSE-data.md (the IMF's terms for statistical data, and CC BY 4.0
    with the World Bank's added terms). This package is not an official IMF or
    World Bank product.
